{"id":"int-11138c0e","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-22T10:55:30.465478966Z","actor":"sorenwilkening","issue_id":"test_C_libtooling-re1","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Prototype validates the no-LLVM-fork architecture claim. cq_pass.cpp (254 LOC) builds against stock LLVM 19.1.7, runs via opt-19 -load-pass-plugin without crash, produces well-formed IR (passes opt -verify), and substitutes all expected lowerings (cq_init_i32→cqrt_alloc_classical_i32, tainted add→cqrt_template_add_i32, cq_measure→cqrt_measure). All 10 smoke-test checks pass. See bd memory prototype-validated-no-fork-2026-05-22."}}
{"id":"int-4d1e4946","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-22T11:10:14.539250398Z","actor":"sorenwilkening","issue_id":"test_C_libtooling-aqf","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Phase 5 prototype validates auto-uncomputation. cq-uncompute pass uses stock LLVM PostDominatorTree (via FunctionAnalysisManagerModuleProxy) to compute the post-dominating last use of each handle, emits cqrt_free at that point, skips handles that escape via ret. Test pipeline: opt-19 -load-pass-plugin -passes='cq-lowering,cq-uncompute' produces 3 cqrt_free calls (one per handle), output passes opt -verify, all checks green. See prototype/test/run_test_phase5.sh, prototype/test/output_phase5.ll."}}
{"id":"int-eaa2cb83","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-22T11:10:19.040878428Z","actor":"sorenwilkening","issue_id":"test_C_libtooling-mh3","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Phase 7 prototype validates call-graph specialization. cq-specialize pass uses stock LLVM CloneFunction (+ ValueToValueMapTy) to clone callees with qint_mid_t-typed args, renames via __cq_q_<f>_q1 mangling, retargets call sites. Test: opt-19 -load-pass-plugin -passes=cq-specialize produces a clone with internal linkage that preserves the original function's body shape (extractvalue + add + insertvalue + ret), call site in @example now references the clone, zero remaining calls to the original from @example, output passes opt -verify. See prototype/test/run_test_phase7.sh, prototype/test/output_phase7.ll."}}
{"id":"int-f8180864","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-22T11:29:17.522682782Z","actor":"sorenwilkening","issue_id":"test_C_libtooling-bhm","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Phase 5 multi-BB validation succeeds. Hand-crafted Stage 4 IR with branch (entry → then/else → merge), one cq_init_i32 in entry, measure in both arms. opt-19 -passes='cq-lowering,cq-uncompute' produces exactly one cqrt_free emitted in the merge block (post-dominator) — not duplicated into either arm. PostDominatorTree.findNearestCommonDominator(then, else) correctly returns merge; getFirstInsertionPt() places the free at the right point (between phi and ret). No code changes were needed — existing computeFreePoint() handles multi-BB correctly. See prototype/test/input_phase5_branch.ll, run_test_phase5_branch.sh."}}
{"id":"int-174c0eb5","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-05-22T11:29:21.793810567Z","actor":"sorenwilkening","issue_id":"test_C_libtooling-dca","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Phase 4 region-handling prototype succeeds. New cq-control pass (~80 LOC) walks each BB tracking cq_when_begin/end bracket state; for each cqrt_template_* call inside a region, substitutes the _controlled variant prepending the control handle. Test verifies: inside-region call replaced, outside-region call preserved, brackets erased, exactly 1 controlled call site + 1 plain call site. Linear single-BB regions only — nested + cross-BB regions deferred but use same stock LLVM API (BasicBlock iteration + IRBuilder + Module.getOrInsertFunction). See prototype/test/input_phase4.ll, run_test_phase4.sh."}}
